{"id":"minicpm5-2b-q8","turns":[{"turn":1,"said":"What shutter speed should I use at 25 frames a second?","kind":"question","expected":"Any answer; nothing changes","passed":true,"failures":[],"credit":1,"reply":"At 25 fps, the camera suggests 1/50 — but that's the default. For video at 25p, faster shutter speeds look choppier and slower look smeary. You'd typically match it to the frame rate using the 180° rule (1/50 at 25 fps). The camera already has 1/50 set, so that's the natural choice.","calls":[],"decisionMs":1191.1232090000003,"totalMs":1191.1459169999998,"steps":1,"generatedTokens":81,"timedOut":false},{"turn":2,"said":"Set the aperture to f/5.6.","kind":"request","expected":"Aperture f/5.6; ISO and shutter unchanged","passed":true,"failures":[],"credit":1,"reply":"Aperture set to f/5.6.","calls":[{"name":"set_setting","arguments":{"setting":"aperture","value":"F5.6"},"valid":true,"changesSomething":true}],"decisionMs":830.9785410000004,"totalMs":1066.0888750000004,"steps":2,"generatedTokens":40,"timedOut":false},{"turn":3,"said":"Is my exposure okay?","kind":"question","expected":"Any answer; nothing changes","passed":true,"failures":[],"credit":1,"reply":"Exposure looks balanced. Mean brightness sits in the middle of the histogram, no clipping, no crushed shadows. You've got 2 stops of headroom to go if you want to expose more to the right.","calls":[{"name":"analyze_frame","arguments":{},"valid":true,"changesSomething":false}],"decisionMs":1561.4466249999996,"totalMs":1561.4574999999995,"steps":2,"generatedTokens":53,"timedOut":false},{"turn":4,"said":"Make it a bit brighter.","kind":"request","expected":"A bit brighter; shutter stays","passed":true,"failures":[],"credit":1,"reply":"Brightened a touch. ISO went up to 1000 to make up for the wider aperture.","calls":[{"name":"adjust_exposure","arguments":{"stops":0.33,"using":"auto"},"valid":true,"changesSomething":true}],"decisionMs":795.7072500000004,"totalMs":1175.2424580000006,"steps":2,"generatedToke